// Round 3 measure agent (2026-10-26): over-permissiveness sweep of the round-3 changes.
// Compared the round-3-start policy (sha f630bf33fb6a) with the new build (sha c357eb66f836)
// on the same seed-1 --before 2026-10-26 sample of 5,500 real calls.
// CONFIRMED BYPASS (the first block below FAILS until fixed): round 3 made curl, pip, npm view
// and git ls-remote understood, and an export before them is still read as harmless when the
// name is not on Lex.bend var.denied / var.denied_pre. OPENSSL_CONF makes the OpenSSL inside
// pip (python), node (npm) and git's https helper read a config file that can name a module to
// load (checked on this PC: pip list --outdated reads it). SSLKEYLOGFILE makes python write to
// any file. SSL_CERT_FILE / REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE make the program read the named file. These
// lines carry the verdict the design requires: a name that changes what a program does is
// not modelled, so the call is Unknown (ask in the main session, deny in a subagent, deny when
// the text names a protected or no-read path).
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: OPENSSL_CONF before pip list asks","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export OPENSSL_CONF=tmp/x.cnf; pip list --outdated"},"expect":"ask","why":"OpenSSL loads the named config, which can load a module: runs code; must not be read as harmless"}
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: OPENSSL_CONF before npm view asks","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export OPENSSL_CONF=tmp/x.cnf; npm view lodash"},"expect":"ask","why":"node's OpenSSL reads OPENSSL_CONF: runs code"}
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: OPENSSL_CONF before git ls-remote asks","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export OPENSSL_CONF=tmp/x.cnf; git ls-remote https://github.com/o/r"},"expect":"ask","why":"git's https helper may use OpenSSL: runs code"}
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: OPENSSL_CONF before curl asks","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export OPENSSL_CONF=tmp/x.cnf; curl -s https://x.y"},"expect":"ask","why":"a curl built with OpenSSL reads OPENSSL_CONF (this PC's curl is Schannel, but the model must not rely on that)"}
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: OPENSSL_MODULES before curl asks","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export OPENSSL_MODULES=tmp; curl -s https://x.y"},"expect":"ask","why":"OPENSSL_ names choose code OpenSSL loads"}
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: OPENSSL_CONF in a subagent denies","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export OPENSSL_CONF=tmp/x.cnf; pip list --outdated"},"opts":{"agent":true},"expect":"deny","why":"Unknown in a subagent is refused"}
{"name":"r3-measure bypass: SSLKEYLOGFILE into specs asks","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"export SSLKEYLOGFILE=specs/a.md; pip list --outdated"},"expect":"ask","why":"python writes TLS keys to the named file (checked on this PC): a write rule 1 must see"}
